<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani yarn rates up, seen rising.</title>
<headline>Pakistani yarn rates up, seen rising.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani cotton yarn rates closed up on Sunday and dealers said prices were likely to rise further amid higher rates in the domestic cotton market.</p>
<p>Rates in rupees supplied by the Pakistan Yarn Merchant Association for a 10-lb (4.54 kg) cone of 21 counts:</p>
<p>				     Sunday	 Previous</p>
<p>    Al-Karam (A.K.)	    445	    435</p>
<p>    Baig (Magic)		 430	    420</p>
<p>    M.G.M.			 435	    425</p>
<p>    ($1 = 40.22 rupees)    -- Ovais Subhani 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
